## Production Deployment Rules
### 1. ALWAYS BACKUP BEFORE OVERWRITING PRODUCTION
Before any file is deployed to the Windows VM (`C:\ClashKing\`), a timestamped backup must be created first:

  ```
  C:\ClashKing\backups\backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS\
  ├── env               (current .env)
  ├── launch_bot.bat    (launcher batch)
  ├── restart_bot.bat   (restart script)
  ├── logs\
  │   └── bot_wrapper.log
  └── src\              (all Python files including .pyc)
  ```

**Implementation:** Use `deploy.py` which calls the backup PowerShell command before any file transfer. Never use `rsync` or `psexec` directly without the backup step first.

  ```powershell
  # Backup command (run via WinRM before any deployment):
  $backupDir = "C:\ClashKing\backups\backup_$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd_HHmmss')"
  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $backupDir -Force
  Copy-Item "C:\ClashKing\src\*" "$backupDir\src\" -Recurse -Force
  Copy-Item "C:\ClashKing\.env" "$backupDir\env" -Force
  Copy-Item "C:\ClashKing\launch_bot.bat" "$backupDir\" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  Copy-Item "C:\ClashKing\restart_bot.bat" "$backupDir\" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path "$backupDir\logs" -Force | Out-Null
  Copy-Item "C:\ClashKing\logs\bot_wrapper.log" "$backupDir\logs\" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  ```

### 2. Rollback Procedure
If a deployment causes issues, the last backup is always available for rollback:

  ```powershell
  $latest = Get-ChildItem "C:\ClashKing\backups" -Directory | Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1
  Copy-Item "$($latest.FullName)\src\*" "C:\ClashKing\src\" -Recurse -Force
  Copy-Item "$($latest.FullName)\env" "C:\ClashKing\.env" -Force
  Copy-Item "$($latest.FullName)\*.bat" "C:\ClashKing\" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  Copy-Item "$($latest.FullName)\logs\bot_wrapper.log" "C:\ClashKing\logs\" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
  ```

### 3. Backup Retention
Keep the last 5 backups automatically. Delete older ones:

  ```powershell
  Get-ChildItem "C:\ClashKing\backups" -Directory | Sort-Object Name | Select-Object -First (Get-ChildItem "C:\ClashKing\backups" -Directory).Count -gt 5 | Select-Object -Skip 5 | Remove-Item -Recurse -Force
  ```

## Project Overview
- **Project:** DiscordCoC (Clash of Clans Clan Discord Server & Bot)
- **Work Item:** #7 (Task)
