## Key Files
- `src/main.py` - Main bot entry point (AliceIsBoredBot class)
- `src/api_client.py` - Supercell API client implementation
- `src/config.py` - Bot configuration (clan tag, API key, region)
- `workitem-7-context.md` - Full work item specification
- `README.md` - Setup and documentation

## Configuration Requirements
- **Bot Token:** Store in `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN` environment variable
- **API Key:** Store in `SUPERCELL_API_KEY` environment variable
- **Clan Tag:** `AliceIsBored` (configurable in config.py)
- **API Region:** Default `eu` (configurable)
- Use `.env` file for local development (see `.env.example`)

## Security Rules
- **Never commit .env files or token values**
- Tokens stored in keyring are encrypted at rest
- When referencing tokens, mask them (e.g., `ghp_****`, `MT****`)
- Only display full tokens when explicitly requested

## Acceptance Criteria (Work Item #7)
- [x] Bot starts and connects to Discord successfully
- [x] Bot responds to ping command
- [x] Supercell API client can fetch clan info by clan tag
- [x] Supercell API client handles rate limiting correctly
- [x] API key and bot token are stored securely (env vars)
- [x] Bot logs API requests and responses (debug level)
- [x] Code is in repository with README for setup
- [x] Azure SQL connected via System-Assigned Managed Identity (`Authentication=ActiveDirectoryMsi`)

## Development Guidelines
- Use Python 3.11+ with virtual environment
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use black for code formatting
- Use pylint for linting
- All API calls must implement rate limiting (max 5 req/sec per Supercell ID)
- Log at DEBUG level for API requests/responses
- **Azure SQL Auth:** Uses SQLAlchemy `creator` function with ODBC `Authentication=ActiveDirectoryMsi` to bypass `Integrated Security` conflict in connection string parsing

